caption: Age of the Hunt
setting-component: age-of-the-hunt

Twenty-five is the Age of the Hunt.

A person younger than 25 is not a valid Blood Moon sacrifice. Upon reaching 25, a person becomes both eligible to participate as a hunter and eligible to be hunted as a sacrifice.

Twenty-five is also the lower limit of Niktul’s rejuvenation blessing. A successful hunter cannot be made biologically younger than 25 by the ordinary Blood Moon reward. Once a hunter reaches biological age 25, additional age-reversal benefits are banked as future unaging: each banked year prevents one future year of biological aging.
